            <ArticleTitle>Opioid, cheating on its receptors, exacerbates pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1465-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Opioids are commonly thought of as compounds that alleviate pain. A new study finds that elevated levels of the opioid dynorphin can unexpectedly activate bradykinin receptors, contributing to the maintenance of neuropathic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
